1
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:07,390
It's 2 a.m. You can't sleep.

2
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,110
Your exam result, your job interview,

3
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:11,010
your business.

4
00:00:11,460 --> 00:00:13,050
What if it doesn't work out?

5
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:19,280
5,000 years ago, the greatest warrior of his time felt the same fear.

6
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:23,590
And Krishna gave him an answer that can change your life too.

7
00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:26,070
Kurukshetra.

8
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,710
Two huge armies face each other.

9
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:29,970
Conches sound.

10
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:32,070
The war is about to begin.

11
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:36,590
In the middle stands one chariot, pulled by white horses.

12
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:38,450
The warrior is Arjuna.

13
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:40,930
His charioteer is Krishna himself.

14
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:45,270
Arjuna looks at the other side and sees his own teachers,

15
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:47,470
his grandfather and his cousins.

16
00:00:47,860 --> 00:00:49,050
His hands shake.

17
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:52,570
His great bow, the Gandiva, slips from his hands.

18
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:55,090
Krishna, I cannot do this.

19
00:00:55,480 --> 00:00:59,130
He is afraid of the war and of what will happen after it.

20
00:00:59,740 --> 00:01:04,290
Krishna turns to him, calm with a gentle smile and he says,

21
00:01:05,620 --> 00:01:07,780
Karmanye Vadhikaraste,

22
00:01:07,970 --> 00:01:09,820
Ma Phaleshu Kadachana.

23
00:01:10,130 --> 00:01:12,320
Ma Karma Phala Hetur Bhur,

24
00:01:12,470 --> 00:01:14,730
Ma Te Sangostva Akarmani.

25
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:18,490
You have a right to your work, but never to its results.

26
00:01:18,820 --> 00:01:23,050
Don't let results be your motive and don't be attached to doing nothing.

27
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:24,860
Lesson one:

28
00:01:25,020 --> 00:01:27,210
Your effort is in your control.

29
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:31,850
A farmer can prepare the soil, plant the seeds and water them every day.

30
00:01:31,940 --> 00:01:33,710
That part is fully his.

31
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:35,610
Lesson two:

32
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:38,050
The result depends on many things.

33
00:01:38,180 --> 00:01:41,570
The farmer can't control the rain, the weather or the market.

34
00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:43,940
If he worries about the rain every night,

35
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:45,850
it doesn't help his crops grow.

36
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:47,890
It only takes away his peace.

37
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:49,820
Lesson three:

38
00:01:50,020 --> 00:01:51,710
Don't run away from action.

39
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:53,890
Krishna isn't saying don't care.

40
00:01:53,940 --> 00:01:58,630
He's telling Arjuna not to let fear of results stop him from doing his duty.

41
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:01,730
And Arjuna stands up again and picks up his bow.

42
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:06,790
If you're a student, focus on today's study,

43
00:02:06,860 --> 00:02:08,110
not tomorrow's marks.

44
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:12,880
If you're working, do today's task well and stop replaying what if.

45
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:15,110
If you're building something, keep building,

46
00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:16,470
one step at a time.

47
00:02:16,620 --> 00:02:18,990
Do your best and let go of the worry.

48
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:23,650
Krishna's words still work, 5,000 years later.

49
00:02:23,780 --> 00:02:25,870
Do your work and leave the worry.

50
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:29,720
If this helped you, subscribe for one lesson from the Gita every week.

51
00:02:29,740 --> 00:02:31,070
Jai Shri Krishna!
